--
KNOWNBUG: N5008 [dcl.spec.auto]/3-4,11 + [temp.variadic]/4-5.  The minimal core
of the std::apply blocker: a function template with a DEDUCED return type
(`decltype(auto)`) whose body calls ANOTHER deduced-return function template,
passing a MULTI-element non-type parameter pack as the arguments
(`decltype(auto) apply_impl(seq<V...>){ return invoke(V...); }` where invoke is
also decltype(auto)).  CBMC leaves the caller's return type an unresolved
`<<type:decltype>>` ("invalid implicit conversion from '<<type:decltype>>' to
'signed int'"; "could not fully type-check 'main'"), so the body is incomplete
and both assertions are skipped -> VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL vacuously, which does
NOT match the desc above (so this correctly registers as a known bug).

Requires ALL of: (1) OUTER return type deduced (auto/decltype(auto), not
trailing decltype); (2) INNER callee a TEMPLATE with a deduced return type (a
concrete decltype(auto) function works); (3) pack size > 1 (a single-element
pack works).  A deduced return type over a pack call to a KNOWN function is
handled (cpp11_auto_return_deduce_pack_call, CORE); the gap is the nested
deduced-return callee whose return type must be deduced during the outer
function's own return-type deduction.  This is the exact error of
cpp17_apply_basic.  g++ runs r == 3; clang++ accepts.  When fixed, the body is
checked, assertion 2 fails, and the desc matches (promote to CORE).
